      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Defining logical processors is hard.  Separate hyperthreads are considered to count but separate execution ports are not....  Cores disabled at the hardware/microcode level don't count, but cores disabled at the kernel/ACPI level do.\n\nIt's basically all a big lie.  It'll become an even bigger lie if hardware starts doing more AMP...  This is one of those cases when the API sorta kinda makes sense in the common case, but defining it rigorously is hard because the entire concept of the API is flaming nonsense in edge cases.\n",
    "created_at": "2016-03-16T13:36:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-16T18:36:14Z",
